From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:25:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Horizon on Linux: NVN draws on a Vulkan GPU

State objects, programs, bindings and the parameters of every draw are recorded and replayed
(nvn_state.py, horizon_nvn.py). Maxwell shaders are translated to SPIR-V by the Ryujinx translator
the Mach host already uses (nvn_spirv.py, built with dotnet for Linux). A headless Vulkan 1.3 device
(linux/host/gpu.c, horizon_gpu.py) renders them into images (nvn_gpu.py), and the frame the window
shows is read back from the GPU. Host functions now receive v0-v7, so float arguments arrive.
NX2LINUX_GPU=1 turns it on. Xenoblade Chronicles 2 draws its title screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: the draws of a recompiled game rendered on a Vulkan GPU (NVN state, Maxwell to SPIR-V, images)
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

